From da0f2202bac986facae9dc866ce4ab9b2bde1da7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:02:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] runtime: composite quad and cylinder layers into each
 eye before encode

The stream carries one projection image per eye, so quads were validated and
dropped and cylinders returned XR_ERROR_LAYER_INVALID: every engine's menus
(UEVR's overlay, Unity, Unreal, Godot) were invisible on the headset.

Session::EndFrame now keeps every quad and cylinder submitted after the
projection layer (back to front) with its last released swapchain snapshot and
a clip-from-layer matrix per eye, built from that eye's own projection view
pose and fov (CompositionOverlay.h). VideoEncoder waits for the overlay
images with the eyes, copies the full eye into the crop texture when an
overlay is visible to it, and OverlayCompositor draws the layers there on the
same command buffer: a quad is one textured quad, a cylinder 8-128 columns;
source-alpha and unpremultiplied flags honoured, sRGB decoded or encoded so
display-encoded bytes keep their value, as the eye conversion already does.
The stream and client are unchanged; overlays reproject with the scene.

XR_KHR_composition_layer_cylinder is advertised. Unknown layer types are
logged once and skipped instead of failing the frame. Not drawn yet:
underlays (layers before the projection), infinite cylinders, equirect.
No mips, so a strongly minified panel aliases.

Cost: VideoEncoder logs encoder command buffer GPU p50/p95 with and without
overlays every 5 s once an overlay has been seen.

Tests: geometry against hand-derived angles (TestCompositionOverlay.cpp) and
GPU pixel checks of position, row order, blend, colour and cylinder span
(TestOverlayCompositor.mm, in the VideoToolbox encoder tests). The encoder
bench target links OverlayCompositor.mm and glm, which VideoEncoder now needs.

